I've seen a lot of Jewish friends who are like, you know, I don't support this. This isn't in alignment with our Jewish principles. This is in alignment with my morals, et cetera, et cetera. And so I think it's important to always note that there are folks who get it. And also understanding that like these histories, I think complex is the wrong word. These histories are recorded. And I think for Black folks, I think a lot of us know that our histories have not been recorded.

